{"title":"2016 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(More_detail)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (More detail)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(CREATIVE_THINKING)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_3(_Easy_Explanation)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 3( Easy Explanation)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Seven cookies of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> inch are cut from a circle of cookie dough, as shown. Neighboring cookies are tangent, and all except the center cookie are tangent to the edge of the dough. The leftover scrap is reshaped to form another cookie of the same thickness. What is the radius in inches of the scrap cookie?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/cca00f7535d16d5f82c2832dbebe7bf865368fed.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw(circle((0,0),3)); draw(circle((0,0),1)); draw(circle((1,sqrt(3)),1)); draw(circle((-1,sqrt(3)),1));  draw(circle((-1,-sqrt(3)),1)); draw(circle((1,-sqrt(3)),1));  draw(circle((2,0),1)); draw(circle((-2,0),1)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/c/7fcbb7fd7d18cc60e3d406ecbff173a20ff8c729.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } \\sqrt{2} \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } 1.5 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } \\sqrt{\\pi} \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } \\sqrt{2\\pi} \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } \\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"427\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The big cookie has radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, since the center of the center cookie is the same as that of the large cookie.  The difference in areas of the big cookie and the seven small ones is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/8404aeb63bf6addd522ee0c0f1792eb3fc654f59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^2\\pi-7\\pi=9\\pi-7\\pi=2 \\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"203\" height=\"18\" />.  The scrap cookie has this area, so its radius must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/c/7cc460410033f9c5b070ae0d022cf6e5f23e232e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }\\sqrt 2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"71\" height=\"33\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28More_detail.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(More_detail)\">Solution 2 (More detail)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (More detail)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We are given the small cookies have a radius of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. This means the radius of the larger cookie is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/a/90a14fecea1f89693b78d459f126fee3e0b2792d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\times 1=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" />. The area of the larger cookie is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/5/81512b65d4f14589a717f1ba14239646bd872c1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi 3^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"17\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/e/f2eddbf4a36b15c84cd5a99fb11d9817bc2978d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9\\pi$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />. The area of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> smaller cookies is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/a/97a3d381541faa0474f0ac82f11fd62785c84906.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7 \\times \\pi 1^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/f/b6feea94b21a7db3646d7529bb4d7d1a0d88a48b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7\\pi$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />. The scrap dough is calculated by subtracting the area of the large cookie by the are of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> small cookies, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/8/158243bbbf16f39cc14919e44e9e366d9db7a0ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9\\pi-7\\pi=2\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"109\" height=\"15\" />. To get the radius, we first divide by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ca003a7da0de4994b4733e203b74ff52d42553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" />, then take the square root of the result, which in this case is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/c/7cc460410033f9c5b070ae0d022cf6e5f23e232e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }\\sqrt 2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"71\" height=\"33\" />. ~<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Shunyipanda&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Shunyipanda (page does not exist)\">shunyipanda</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28CREATIVE_THINKING.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(CREATIVE_THINKING)\">Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/1ocp50QWOzU\">https://youtu.be/1ocp50QWOzU</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1\">Video Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/dHY8gjoYFXU?t=1290\">https://youtu.be/dHY8gjoYFXU?t=1290</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/NsQbhYfGh1Q?t=899\">https://youtu.be/NsQbhYfGh1Q?t=899</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_3.28_Easy_Explanation.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_3(_Easy_Explanation)\">Video Solution 3( Easy Explanation)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 3( Easy Explanation)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Xa61-YgFo4Y\">https://youtu.be/Xa61-YgFo4Y</a>\n</p>\n<h2><